      "writtenOn": "2019-10-10T02:55:03Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "OpenSSL 1.0 was only working for little-endian architectures (x86) and had direct access to BIGNUM structure, so DCRYPTO_bn_wrap which just sets a pointer to user provided buffer as source for LITE_BIGNUM could be applied data in BIGNUM extracted by memcpy(). In OpenSSL 1.1 BIGNUM became opaque, so we need to use extra code to get data in little-endian format which used by DCRYPTO_*. It\u0027s actually replacement for memcpy()",
